:"Rwanda","min_lon":28.805192026702148,"min_lat":-2.92173806576367,"max_lon":30.8892317148125,"max_lat":-1.15476480869885,"source_file":"world_2010.geojson","source_row":null}],"identities":[{"qid":"Q889884","from_t":1945,"to_t":1962,"method":"name-template+date","confidence":0.840051499783199,"label":"Kingdom of Rwanda","description":"former kingdom in East Africa from the 15th century and up to 1962","inception":null,"dissolved":1962.4931506849316,"enwiki":"Kingdom of Rwanda","summary":"The Kingdom of Rwanda (also known as the Nyiginya Kingdom or Nyginya Dynasty) was a Bantu kingdom in modern-day Rwanda which grew to be ruled by a Tutsi monarchy. It was one of the most centralized kingdoms in Central and East Africa. It was later annexed under German and Belgian colonial rule while retaining some of its autonomy. The Tutsi monarchy was abolished in 1961 after ethnic violence erupted between the Hutu and the Tutsi during the Rwandan Revolution, which started in 1959."},{"qid":"Q1037","from_t":1962,"to_t":2020,"method":"name-label+date","confidence":0.95,"label":"Rwanda","description":"country in East Africa","inception":1962,"dissolved":null,"enwiki":"Rwanda","summary":"Rwanda, officially the Republic of Rwanda, is a landlocked country in East Africa. Its geography is dominated by mountains in the west and savanna in the southeast. The largest and most notable lakes are mainly in the western and northern regions of the country, and several volcanoes that form part of the Virunga volcanic chain are primarily in the northwest. The climate is considered tropical highland, with two rainy seasons and two dry seasons each year."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q889884","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q528679","value_label":"Nyanza","from_t":1899,"to_t":1961.0739726027398,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Nyanza"},{"qid":"Q889884","kind":"language","value_qid":"Q33573","value_label":"Kinyarwanda","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P2936","retri