nda","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Juvénal Habyarimana"},{"qid":"Q1037","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q471882","value_label":"Pasteur Bizimungu","from_t":1994.545205479452,"to_t":2000.224043715847,"title":"President of Rwanda","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Pasteur Bizimungu"},{"qid":"Q1037","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q557995","value_label":"Grégoire Kayibanda","from_t":1961.8164383561643,"to_t":1973.5068493150684,"title":"President of Rwanda","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Grégoire Kayibanda"},{"qid":"Q1037","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q888396","value_label":"Dominique Mbonyumutwa","from_t":1961.0739726027398,"to_t":1961.8164383561643,"title":"President of Rwanda","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Dominique Mbonyumutwa"},{"qid":"Q1037","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q888967","value_label":"Théodore Sindikubwabo","from_t":1994.2657534246575,"to_t":1994.545205479452,"title":"President of Rwanda","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Théodore Sindikubwabo"},{"qid":"Q1037","kind":"flag","value_qid":"Q170543","value_label":"Flag of Rwanda.svg","from_t":2001.813698630137,"to_t":null,"title":"flag of Rwanda","property":"P163","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"flag of Rwanda"}],"people":{"Q1231345":{"label":"Paul Kagame","description":"President of Rwanda since 2000 (born 1957)","enwiki":"Paul Kagame","summary":"Paul Kagame (born 23 October 1957) is a Rwandan politician and former military officer who has been the president of Rwanda since 2000. He is considered to be Rwanda's de facto leader since 1994, from 1994 till 2000 while Vice President and Minister of Defence under President Pasteur Bizimungu. He was previously a commander of the Rwandan Patriotic Front (RPF), a rebel armed force which invaded Rwanda in 1990. The RPF was one of the main belligerents of the Rwandan Civil War and was the armed force which ended the 1994 Rwandan genocide.","image":"Paul Kagame 2024 (cropped).jpg","birth":1957.8082191780823,"death":null},"Q135454730":{"label":"Justin Nsengiyumva","description":"prime minister of Rwanda","enwiki":"Justin Nsengiyumva","summary":"Justin Nsengiyumva (born (1971-10-10)10 October 1971) is a Rwandan banker and politician serving as the current Prime Minister of Rwanda since 25 July 2025.","image":"Justin Nsengiyumva in June 2026 (cropped).jpg","birth":1971.772602739726,"death":null},"Q272580":{"label":"Juvénal Habyarimana","description":"2nd President of Rwanda (1937–1994)","enwiki":"Juvénal Habyarimana","summary":"Juvénal Habyarimana (Kinyarwanda: [hɑβɟɑːɾímɑ̂ːnɑ]; French: [ʒyvenal abjaʁimana]; 8 March 1937 – 6 April 1994) was a Rwandan politician and military dictator who was the second president of Rwanda, from 1973 until his assassination in 1994.\nAn ethnic Hutu, Habyarimana served in several security positions in the First Rwandese republic including minister of defense under Rwanda's second president, Grégoire Kayibanda. After overthrowing Kayibanda in a coup in 1973, he became the country's new president of the Second Rwandese Republic. Habyarimana later continued his predecessor's pro-Hutu policies.","image":"Juvénal Habyarimana (1980).jpg","birth":1937.1808219178083,"death":1994.2602739726028},"Q471882":{"label":"Pasteur Bizimungu","description":"Rwandan politician, 3rd and former President of Rwanda","enwiki":"Pasteur Bizimungu","summary":"Pasteur Bizimungu (born 30 April 1950) is a Rwandan politician who served as the third President of Rwanda, holding office from 19 July 1994 until 23 March 2000.\nBizimungu had previously held several positions under President Juvenal Habyarimana throughout the 1980s. He joined the Rwandan Patriotic Front (RPF) rebel group against Habyarimana in 1990 following the death of his brother seemingly under the orders of Habyarimana's government. After the RPF's victory in the Rwandan Civil War in 1994 which ended the Rwandan genocide, Bizimungu became the new president of the country with RPF commander Paul Kagame as vice-president and minister of defense, who was seen as the country's de facto leader throughout his presidency.","image":"Pasteur Bizimungu 1998 (cropped).jpg","birth":1950.2465753424658,"death":null},"Q557995":{"label":"Grégoire Kayibanda","description":"Rwandan politician, 1st and former President of Rwanda (1924-1976)","enwiki":"Grégoire Kayibanda","summary":"Grégoire Kayibanda (1 May 1924 – 15 December 1976) was a Rwandan politician, revolutionary and military dictator who was the first President of Rwanda from 1962 to 1973. An ethnic Hutu, he was a pioneer of the Rwandan Revolution and led Rwanda's struggle for independence from Belgium, replacing the Tutsi monarchy with the First Rwandese Republic. Rwanda became independent from Belgium in 1962, with Kayibanda serving as the country's first president, establishing a pro-Hutu policy and a de facto one-party system governed by his party, Parmehutu. He was overthrown in a coup d'état in 1973 by his defense minister, Juvénal Habyarimana, and died three years later.","image":"1649592763733 19650300 RWANDA 45.jpg","birth":1924.3306010928961,"death":1976.9535519125684},"Q888396":{"label":"Dominique Mbonyumutwa","description":"Rwandan president (1921-1986)","enwiki":"Dominique Mbonyumutwa","summary":"Dominique Mbonyumutwa (January 1921 – 26 July 1986) was a Rwandan politician who served as the interim first President of Rwanda for a period of nine months in 1961, during a transitional phase between the overthrow of the Rwandan monarchy in the Rwandan Revolution and the country's independence. Following an election in October of that year, he was succeeded by Grégoire Kayibanda who became the first elected president of the country following independence.","image":null,"birth":1921,"death":1986.5643835616438},"Q888967":{"label":"Théodore Sindikubwabo","description":"Rwandan politician interine (1928-1998)","enwiki":"Théodore Sindikubwabo","summary":"Théodore Sindikubwabo (1928 – March 1998) was a Rwandan politician who was the interim President of Rwanda during the Rwandan genocide, from 8 April to 19 July 1994. Prior to that, he was President of the Rwandan legislature National Development Council from 1988–1994.\nSindikubwabo was born in Zivu, Shyanda village, in the town of Butare, formerly called Astrida in Rwanda-Urundi Territory, and currently the southern province of Rwanda.  Sindikubwabo was educated as a physician and was Minister of Health in the administration of President Kayibanda.","image":null,"birth":1928,"death":1998.1616438356164}},"media":{"Flag of Rwanda (January – September 1961).svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Flag_of_Rwanda_%28January_%E2%80%93_September_1961%29.svg/330px-Flag_of_Rwanda_%28January_%E2%80%93_September_1961%29.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Rwanda_(January_%E2%80%93_September_1961).svg","author":"Unknown sourceUnknown source","license":"Public domain"},"Royal coat of arms of Rwanda.png":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Royal_coat_of_arms_of_Rwanda.png/330px-Royal_coat_of_arms_of_Rwanda.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_coat_of_arms_of_Rwanda.png","author":"Poohgun - junmon","license":"Public domain"},"Flag of Rwanda.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Flag_of_Rwanda.svg/330px-Flag_of_Rwanda.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Rwanda.svg","author":"Original: Unknown Vector:  Zscout370","license":"Public domain"},"Coat of arms of Rwanda.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Coat_of_arms_of_Rwanda.svg/330px-Coat_of_arms_of_Rwanda.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imagei